# Firebase Android config — injected at build time from the GOOGLE_SERVICES_JSON secret, never committed.
clients/android-phone/app/google-services.json

# Deno lockfile — generated by local type-checking, not part of the edge build
deno.lock

# Portable analytics report QA writes failure-only screenshots beside the report.
*.verification-failure.png
verify-debug.png

# Superdesign scratch components and generated prompt payloads.
.superdesign/tmp/

# Local browser/emulator QA evidence. Curated evidence belongs under docs/audits/.
.playwright-cli/
test-results/
output/

# Hetzner operational snapshots can contain live credentials. Keep the
# versioned redacted example, but never allow timestamped env/script/compose
# backups or media env files into Git.
ops/hetzner/.env.bak-*
ops/hetzner/media/.env.*
ops/hetzner/**/*.bak-*
ops/hetzner/.env.backup-*
# The dot form too. The rules above only caught .env.bak-* with a hyphen, so
# backups named .env.bak.<date> — which is what a cp during an incident
# actually produces — stayed untracked AND unignored, exactly the situation the
# note below describes. These files carry every secret in the stack, not just
# the one being rotated.
ops/hetzner/.env.bak.*
ops/hetzner/.env.*.bak
ops/hetzner/**/*.bak
# Ceinture et bretelles pour le fichier temporaire de
# provision-abuse-signup-secrets.sh. Il doit vivre dans le même répertoire que
# le .env, sinon le mv final n'est pas atomique — rename ne traverse pas les
# systèmes de fichiers. Il naît en 600, un trap le retire, et cette règle couvre
# le cas où le processus est tué entre les deux. Les SAUVEGARDES, elles, ne sont
# plus ici du tout : elles vont dans ~/.norva-secret-backups, parce qu'une règle
# .gitignore ne protège pas d'un `git add -f`, d'un tar, d'un rsync ni de
# quelqu'un qui lit simplement le working tree.
ops/hetzner/.env.tmp.*
# Backup archives must never land in the repo (audit 2026-08-20 : un .tar.gz.age
# de 849 Mo et deux .env de secrets tramaient non suivis ET non ignores).
*.age
norva-db-*.tar.gz*
norva-selfhost-*.tar.gz*

# Generated Kong declarative config: scripts/00-generate-kong.sh substitutes the
# real anon/service_role JWTs and the dashboard password into it. The committed
# artefact is the template under ops/hetzner/volumes/api/, which holds only $VAR
# placeholders. Left untracked AND unignored, one `git add -A` would have
# published live database credentials into the repository.
ops/hetzner/kong/
